+When an image's built-in Docker healthcheck targets a different internal port,
+declare a bounded HTTP override in the recipe:
+
+```toml
+[recipe.serve.healthcheck]
+mode = "http"
+port = 30123
+path = "/health"
+interval_seconds = 15
+timeout_seconds = 5
+start_period_seconds = 600
+retries = 5
+```
+
+`port` is the in-container probe port and is independent of the loopback-published
+`recipe.serve.port`. The path must be a normalized absolute HTTP path. Load renders
+the validated target as Docker health options without host-shell interpolation;
+unknown fields, modes other than `http`, invalid ports or paths, and out-of-range
+timings fail before Docker starts. If the table is absent, the image's healthcheck
+behavior is inherited unchanged. The runtime image must provide `curl` for an
+explicit HTTP healthcheck.
+
 ```bash
 anvil-serving models recipes create --recipe-file ./candidate-recipe.toml --registry ./serve-recipes.local.toml --dry-run
 anvil-serving models recipes create --recipe-file ./candidate-recipe.toml --registry ./serve-recipes.local.toml --confirm
