+### Build a derived image
+
+When a model requires a pinned local derivative, declare its build context in the
+operator recipe rather than running an ad hoc Docker command:
+
+```toml
+[recipe.image_build]
+context = "derived-images/model-runtime"
+dockerfile = "Dockerfile"
+pull = true
+platform = "linux/amd64"
+
+[recipe.serve]
+image = "anvil-serving/model-runtime:upstream-revision"
+```
+
+Both paths are normalized relative paths. The context must remain below the
+directory containing the operator registry; symbolic links and empty contexts
+fail closed. The target image must be a tag, not a mutable implicit `latest` or
+a digest-only reference. Pin every external base and downloaded source inside
+the Dockerfile.
+
+```bash
+anvil-serving models recipes build-image MODEL --registry ./serve-recipes.local.toml --dry-run
+anvil-serving models recipes build-image MODEL --registry ./serve-recipes.local.toml --confirm
+```
+
+Preview records the context-tree, Dockerfile, and recipe SHA-256 digests, the
+previous target image ID, exact `docker build` argv, and a tag-restore command.
+Apply recomputes those inputs after confirmation, builds without loading a
+model, then inspects the target and requires Anvil's model, recipe, and context
+provenance labels. The prior image is not deleted, and the operation never
+changes a serve, route, or promotion state.
 
